== (i) centrality: the P9 clause in algebraic form ==
  [V_(3,2)^even, (-1)^F] = 0.0e+00   (commutes exactly)
  V_(3,0)^odd: commutator norm = 2.0, anticommutator = 0.0e+00
  -> the grading is CENTRAL in the record algebra (P9's
     univalence superselection); the odd seal fails
     centrality and is excluded from the ledger ALGEBRAICALLY
     - the blocking table's P9 rows are now one commutator.

== (ii) the collapse: commutant counting and equivalence ==
  small ledger Z6 x Z4 (exact linear algebra):
   commutant dim without seal: 48   (= 48 labels)
   with the even (3,2)-seal:   24   (expected 24 = orbits x grading)
   label counting: PASS
  full ledger Z12 x Z8: orbits of +(3,2) = 24  -> 48 labels with grading
  distinct (tau, sigma, Y6 mod 24) labels: 24  (= 24: complete invariants)
  charges (0,0) and (3,2): SAME A-module (orbit block): True
  charge (1,0): different block; nearest spectral gap to
  the (0,0)-block = 0.246 > 0 (inequivalent modules)
  -> the seal makes charges (0,0) and (3,2) ONE
     superselection class (the same cyclic module of the
     sealed algebra); classes off the orbit stay distinct:
     the collapse lemma's GNS argument, live.

== (iii) the control: a second seal kills the functional ==
  small ledger, seals (3,2) AND (0,2): commutant dim = 12   (expected 12)
  full ledger orbits with both seals: 6  (vs 24 with one)
  -> further collapse: with rank-2 screening only finitely
     many labels survive and every continuous functional
     dies - the L3 mechanism, live in the toy.

== (iv) nonvanishing on every background (toy E-bg) ==
  ||V_(3,2) psi_q|| over all backgrounds: min = 1.0, max = 1.0
  -> the seal acts isometrically on every charge background
     in the toy.  In the real ledger this is the (E-bg)
